// Mirrors the source's own assertFalse: a member of one group_with_parent
// (analysis) should never view a document shared only with a distinct
// sibling group (engineering), even though both share a common parent.
//
// Before `docs/DECISIONS.md`'s entry adding `NeverRelationConstraint`,
// this invariant's own real verdict was VIOLATED: nothing stopped the
// search from adding one more, wholly unconstrained direct grant of
// `document.viewer` (bare principal) to `a` — the exact "recurring
// finding" `docs/FINDINGS.md` disclosed. A second, structurally
// different escape survived even after excluding that one specific
// grant (D-131's own narrow primitive): `group_with_parent.member`'s own
// recursive `parent`-chain, reachable via a completely fresh,
// unconstrained group never named by this invariant at all.
// `never document#viewer(a)` and `never group_with_parent#member(a)`
// close both — the second line closes the recursive chain at every
// depth, since every step of `parent->member` still has to resolve
// `group_with_parent.member`'s own direct edge somewhere. `a`'s real,
// legitimate membership in `analysis` (this invariant's own given
// premise) is exempted, not blocked — see `NeverRelationConstraint`'s
// own doc comment for why that exemption is what makes this sound
// rather than self-contradictory. See `docs/FINDINGS.md` for the full
// account.
invariant sibling_group_member_cannot_view_other_group_document {
  a: user
  analysis: group_with_parent
  engineering: group_with_parent
  d: document

  member(analysis) = a
  viewer_group(d) = engineering
  distinct(analysis, engineering)

  never document#viewer(a)
  never group_with_parent#member(a)

  goal: view(a, d)
}
